t but that's it's not the  case the team is the one that's carrying  the torch forward and  they always have been the overwatch team  was started in 2013.  our senior leadership group they're all  original members  of that team we have so many people that  started this project that are still  there and then we have brought  so many other people on that are now  like  these incredibly impactful creative  members of the team  and all of us together are the ones that  are that are bringing this forward and  i'm just happy  that i'm able to play whatever role in  it that i can  naturally the big question around  keller's appointment is whether things  are going to change drastically  people tend to ascribe a vision around a  game to one person  in the case of overwatch that person was  jeff kaplan  so does keller have his own ideas that  he wants to implement  i was lucky enough to be in a role  previous to this  where i was really well connected and  aligned to what the vision  for both overwatch one and overwatch two  were coming into a position like i'm in  right now  um we're mid-cycle on overwatch too i  don't think it's right  for me to suddenly make a bunch of big  changes  to to either one of these games  um and and i think what's nice is  there aren't really huge changes that i  that i do want to make to either game  because i've been so involved in  in both of them among fans one point of  discussion is the pace at which  overwatch content and updates are  delivered next to games like fortnite  call of duty war zone apex legends and  other big multiplayer experiences  overwatch moves at a glacial pace  looking forward with the aforementioned  games as competition  are there plans to speed things up  according to keller  quality is the priority but blizzard  knows things need to be quicker  and it needs to hold on to content a  little less yeah one of the  the values that that blizzard has is  this commit to quality  um and we're always looking to make the  very  best version of anything that that we  make but i think that there can be a  tendency to  cling to that and maybe hold on to  pieces  of content or systems that we made  longer than we should  we are going to make a great game and we  are really committed  to making it as amazing as we possibly  can and the last thing we want to do  is to release it early before it's ready  but we recognize that it's something  that  players are waiting for and it's  something that's important to put out  there  so we are doing as much as we possibly  can to accelerate the development  process for it  i think that this is something that when  i start looking forward  um just personally on what i think we  ought to be doing in the future  it's really important for the game and  for the community for us to be  releasing as much as we possibly can for  the game  of course one of the ways popular modern  games keep people engaged is through  things like a battle pass  and almost weekly updates something that  wasn't the case for overwatch  as a result there's been some discussion  about overwatch 2 needing to behave more  like other live service games if only to  ensure that the player base stays  healthy  while keller didn't say whether the  seeker will have features that have  become commonplace in other live service  games  he did indicate that having a lot of  content is important  i i can't really speak to exactly what  will be in there whether this game's  going to have  a battle pass or not but i think i can  talk to our values a little bit because  um when we when we design anything at  blizzard we like to set up the the  values for the pillars for it and then  everything kind of derives  from from those particular values and  the values for  overwatch too is that we we want the  game to  to feel like it has a constant heartbeat  um  that there's um a lot of updates to the  game and that the community knows that  um that it's kind of our first priority  um moving forward so it's hard for me to  say like every live game is a little  different  whether the value is a live service  value i think our value  is to put as much time and resources as  we can  into updating the live game into making  it always feel  kind of like new and fresh and  substantial  talking about the new pve mode the  so-called second part of overwatch 2's  experience  keller said that this mode was important  for people that might not be as  dedicated to competitive gaming  but still have a lot of love for the  game world and characters  as a result is something that the  development team is committed to  supporting what i'm hoping  is that going forward overwatch 2 can be  that game  that is played by a much broader section  of the community  i want the game to be just as  competitive if not  more so on the pvp side we have a lot of  really exciting things that we're doing  to i think  kind of shake up the way pvp is played  to  innovate on what we've done um and to  bring  you know new new game modes and really  interesting ways of playing to the table  but at the same time we want this way  for these people that  just love this world and its heroes to  be able to play the game  as well and and to to come away with um  like a really  um special um story and a deeper  understanding of what that world is and  that's what  this other side of the game is that  we're building or the pvp side of  development is something that  i think is incredibly streamlined across  the team  and it is something that we're experts  at i recognize  that the other side of the game is  it's a big undertaking and there's more  to it than than building  um the pvp side of the game and i think  the game that we've talked about  is um it's a content based game when you  start talking about  progression systems especially deep  progression systems you need a lot of  content  in order to be able to deliver like a  really great experience for players to  to work through that we have a lot of  people  on our team that have worked on  a lot of different projects throughout  the industry and a lot of different  games in blizzard we have a lot of  people from the world of warcraft team  from the diablo team and even from the  starcraft team and i think  that we all recognize the type of game  that we're building  and we're building all of the right  systems and the right content  in order to make it um really really  engaging and fun for players  so um i agree with you it's a it's a big  ask but i think that we're  we're set up and we're approaching it  eyes wide open knowing what it what it  needs to  to deliver on that so what about  becoming aaron keller from the overwatch  team  kaplan was a public presence the subject  of memes goofs and guests  is that something that keller wants or  needs to be and what is it like to have  that expectation on him from the  community  it's important for us to to um  communicate with our community  i i can't speak to exactly what um  all of the updates were look like um or  what the the  the ways that we communicate are going  to be we're we're talking about  um several things right now that we're  going to be doing going forward  but i i'm not exactly sure what form all  of them are going to take  but yes i will be talking to to the  community  we have every intention of remaining in  communication  with our community what that looks like  whether that's always me or not  i think is probably best left as a  process  rather than a decision i i guess what i  mean by that is  i think jeff was a little uncomfortable  as as the person out in front of the  overwatch team it was his  value that as much of the spotlight  could could be um put on the team itself  he ended up kind of kind of becoming  more and more focused on  um over time and i don't think there's  anything wrong with that  i think it worked out well for us but it  doesn't have to be that way i don't  have to be the person that's always  communicating  our our thoughts and intentions if it  ends up happening that way  it it will end up happening that way but  it could also be other people on the  team that are taking up that mantle i  think  the value here is that we continue  communicating  with our community the value isn't that  it has to be me  doing it teams especially like a  creative team a game development team  they're very organic structures and  um they're they're entirely formed  around  the strengths and weaknesses and  personalities of everybody on that team  from  um the newest members of the team to  to some of the the most senior people on  the team  um and a lot of times what happens  when somebody leaves a team especially  somebody in a leadership role  is everyone expects the new person  to just jump in and do everything that  the that that the person  that their predecessor was doing so in a  very real sense  we have a jeff shaped hole on our team  right now  but i'm not jeff i'm not i don't have  all the same strengths and weaknesses  that jeff has i have a different  leadership style  than jeff has um and so i think  going forward um things will look a  little different  across the team things will look a  little different the way  in our communication style to the  community  and there's nothing wrong with that it's  very natural  for for something like that to happen  every game director  that i know i've worked with has a  slightly different focus  um jeff was a vice president in  at blizzard and his focus um was really  wide and  he was also incredibly capable  of handling a wide focus and looking at  at  not just the team but different parts of  the organization  my mandate and some of this is  self-imposed  um some of this is in conversations with  other people across the company the team  is to focus as much as possible  on overwatch as a game that's where i'm  going to be pouring  my creative energy and passion and time  building that it's so interesting too  because  i think you could see jeff's love for  the game  in everything that he did um and  i i just really hope that going forward  the the community realizes that  not just me but everyone else on the  team shares that  um you know we're like we're developers  at blizzard entertainment where  like highly valued in the industry and  we could  typically go and work anywhere we want  to  but this is what we're choosing to work  on because  this is the game that we all love  does this mean overwatch is back  yes we are  [Music]  thanks for watching this video about  overwatch 2's new game director aaron  keller  this is actually a shortened down  version of the full interview which you  can read on gamespot.com  make sure to check it out because  there's a lot more details about the  future of overwatch 2 to managing the  team  and charting the past for the future of  the franchise you can find me on twitter  tomorrhege and i'll see you next time  you

